# Google Cloud inventory

## Gate

Use when the user asks which project is active, to list projects or top-level
resources, or to resolve a named GCP id before further work. Skip bare
"Google Cloud" with no project or inventory ask.

## Transport

No Google Cloud MCP was discovered for this harness. Prefer authenticated
`gcloud` (Application Default Credentials or an active `gcloud auth` login).
If a Cloud MCP appears later, use its list/describe tools when ready —
**do not invent MCP tool names**.

## Resolve project

1. Prefer an exact project id the user named this turn.
2. Else read the active config: `gcloud config get-value project`.
3. Else list candidates: `gcloud projects list --format='table(projectId,name,projectNumber)'`.
4. Confirm with `gcloud projects describe PROJECT_ID` before mutate or
   claiming ownership.
5. Do **not** run `gcloud config set project` unless the user named the
   target project and asked to switch.

Never invent billing accounts, org ids, folder ids, or project ids.

## Auth and config (read-only)

| Need | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Active project | `gcloud config get-value project` |
| Account in use | `gcloud config get-value account` |
| Config list | `gcloud config list` |
| Auth list (emails only) | `gcloud auth list` |
| ADC present? | `gcloud auth application-default print-access-token` only to verify; **never paste the token** |

## Project / org inventory

| Need | Command |
| --- | --- |
| List projects | `gcloud projects list` |
| Describe project | `gcloud projects describe PROJECT_ID` |
| Enabled APIs | `gcloud services list --enabled --project=PROJECT_ID` |
| Billing link (metadata) | `gcloud billing projects describe PROJECT_ID` |

Keep receipts short: project id + name + (optional) number. Do not dump full
org trees or billing account secrets.

## Region / zone orientation

When compute or GKE work follows, state region or zone from the ask or from
a prior list — do not guess `us-central1-a`. Useful reads:

- `gcloud compute regions list` / `gcloud compute zones list` (filter when
  the user named a region)
- `gcloud config get-value compute/region` / `compute/zone` when set

## Defaults

1. Prefer list/describe over create when the ask is “what do we have”.
2. State project + region/zone in every receipt that touches resources.
3. Cap listings (page size / `--limit` / filters) — do not flood chat with
   hundreds of rows; summarize and offer a tighter filter.
4. Workspace mail/docs/Drive are out of scope for this plugin.

## Refuse

- Inventing billing accounts, org ids, or folder paths.
- Dumping `gcloud auth` tokens, refresh tokens, or ADC JSON into chat.
- Switching the active project without an explicit switch ask + target id.
- Claiming a project exists without a list/describe this turn.
